1. Program execution starts from EncapsulationHiding2.main().

2. Object is created:
      EncapsulationHiding1 obj = new EncapsulationHiding1();

3. Memory is allocated for:
      name
      age
      course
      duration

4. Setter methods are called:
      setName("Bhaskar")
      setAge(25)
      setCourse("Java")
      setDuration(7.5")

   These methods store values into the private variables.

5. Getter methods are called:
      getName()
      getAge()
      getCourse()
      getDuration()

   These methods return the stored values.

6. Returned values are printed on the console.

