Important Interview Points
--------------------------

// Data Hiding:
// ------------
// Making variables private so they cannot be accessed directly
// from outside the class.

// Encapsulation:
// --------------
// Binding variables and methods into a single unit (class)
// and providing controlled access using getters and setters.

// Setter Method:
// --------------
// Used to assign or update the value of a private variable.

// Getter Method:
// --------------
// Used to retrieve the value of a private variable.

// Why use getters and setters?
// ----------------------------
// 1. Protects data.
// 2. Allows validation.
// 3. Controls read/write access.
// 4. Improves maintainability.
// 5. Follows Object-Oriented Programming principles.























